08da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=circuit.helper_contraction&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=circuit.helper_contraction&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=circuit.helper_contraction&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&ref=sha256%3A9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.helper_contraction","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"First fix the finite input channels and surrounding word. Helper pinning concerns all helper descendants, not only the receiver root. Individual approximating commutator factors need not preserve that subspace. Lower first responses and scalar second responses must be retained; covariance between channels cannot be discarded.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-helper-contraction"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.helper_contraction","kind":"claim","label":"Pinned helpers implement propagation through contraction","locator":"04-classical-synthesis.tex:207–959; prop:helper-contraction, eq:helper-pinning-projection, eq:diagonal-helper-paths, eq:limiting-additive-response","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-synthesis","statement":"Fix a finite surrounding gate-calculus word avoiding an unused positive-probability helper mask K. For disjoint receiver I and sender J with excluded seed-only bounded odd transmitted f, refine J into J_l and use the I–J_l–K–J_l commutator paths with the 1/p_K factor. On the recursively compressed space pinning X=1 at every helper descendant, finitely many such propagations converge simultaneously as max_l p_l→0. Backtracking terms supply the wanted propagation; distinct-sender terms vanish by orthogonal mask bounds. Root maps and adjoints converge conditionally modulo harmless root-seed phases; off-helper insertions converge.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.helper_contraction","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.helper_contraction","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.helper_contraction%22%2C%22circuit.additive_responses%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.helper_contraction%22%2C%22circuit.additive_responses%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.additive_responses"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.helper_contraction","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.helper_contraction%22%2C%22circuit.gate_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.helper_contraction%22%2C%22circuit.gate_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.gate_calculus"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.helper_contraction","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.helper_contraction%22%2C%22circuit.orthogonal_quadratics%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a